From: Cursor Agent <cursoragent@cursor.com>
Date: Wed, 14 Oct 2026 03:45:36 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 2/4] docs(architecture): align the architecture with ADR-013,
 ADR-014 and 1.1.0

Several statements contradicted accepted decisions or the merged
implementation. The ADR table stopped at ADR-013 and said 13 ADRs
while ADR-014 (API keys bound to tenants) was accepted; 3.1, 4.2 and
16.1 still named PostgreSQL as the authoritative store, against the
SQLite first order of ADR-013; 5.5 asked for multi-instance
controllers, which the single-writer phase forbids; 17.1, which the
README calls the authoritative repository structure, listed design
documents and directories that do not exist and missed scripts/,
docs/governance, docs/releases, a plugin and most gateway packages;
and 19 read as the current plan.

Correct those, and record what 1.1.0 implements where the design
describes it: the API surface, authentication and the error envelope
(13.1), the event envelope and its delivery guarantees (13.2), the
gateway's forwarding rules (14.1) and the metrics and trace context
(15.1, 16.1). Section 19 is marked as the original plan, and 20 points
to the roadmap's acceptance table.
